# Geometry

- Coordinates: origin at wall × top of lower shelf; +X into the room; +Y up; millimeters.
- Model the LED as one or more emit surfaces of `led.width` (W). Sample ends plus ≥16 interior points on every segment or arc.
- Mount types are distinct: `downward` (horizontal window under the upper shelf) and valance-flush `radius` / `ell` / `triangle`.
- Occluders are solid bodies: upper shelf, lower shelf, valance (бленда), and the opaque `ell` body. Edge graze counts as blocked.
- Direct glare exists if any emit-point → eye segment is unobstructed and in that surface's front half-plane.
- Do not replace the segment test with a single worst-case point. The inner edge can glare when looking up under the shelf.
